{"timestamp":"2026-09-29T11:18:39.607Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"d7765680-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"one-shot-brief-v1\",\n  \"subject\": \"Pregnancy health and wellbeing\",\n  \"lessonTitle\": \"Ten habits for a healthier, calmer pregnancy\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Move your body through pregnancy, with gentle trimester-appropriate activity like a 10-minute walk in the first trimester to support circulation, blood sugar, and labor endurance.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"cb8f7d55-9457-7a36-a94d-f38c7571c618\", \"604275ae-a74d-7c42-bad4-13827eb8f178\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Eat protein at every meal to stay full longer, steady blood sugar, and supply amino acids for growth and development.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"a37b4fac-db6d-7d25-8f7a-48e904acfb30\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Take prenatal vitamins at night with food to reduce iron-related nausea and stomach discomfort.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"59dbe5f6-0184-79af-a5dd-da2722639ef0\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Keep a journal to capture emotions, fears, questions, and milestones that photos alone cannot preserve.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"97f49124-75e3-7fb1-9205-3444500c8dfc\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Stop Googling symptoms at 2 a.m.; instead learn the true red flags (severe headache, vision changes, chest pain, breathing difficulty, sudden swelling, leaking) and rely on one trusted source rather than crowdsourced opinions.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"c7ebf55b-20cf-7847-b79c-27717f99ac75\", \"20d30df4-3381-7d51-bf3b-9d55dbf55070\", \"629724df-097b-7fbc-bd4e-8043aa2e7a64\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Learn what your body will actually do in labor - stages, contractions, and normal progression - to reduce fear and feel prepared.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"16bc9d5a-ca5e-7b42-86f4-25a2880e159d\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Train your pelvic floor for both strength and relaxation so you move from passenger to participant during birth.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"aae36a14-0570-75c5-88a4-48c13a0a35ec\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Start planning for postpartum now: recovery, sleep disruption, hormonal shif","textChunks":["{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"one-shot-brief-v1\",\n  \"subject\": \"Pregnancy health and wellbeing\",\n  \"lessonTitle\": \"Ten habits for a healthier, calmer pregnancy\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Move your body through pregnancy, with gentle trimester-appropriate activity like a 10-minute walk in the first trimester to support circulation, blood sugar, and labor endurance.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"cb8f7d55-9457-7a36-a94d-f38c7571c618\", \"604275ae-a74d-7c42-bad4-13827eb8f178\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Eat protein at every meal to stay full longer, steady blood sugar, and supply amino acids for growth and development.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"a37b4fac-db6d-7d25-8f7a-48e904acfb30\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Take prenatal vitamins at night with food to reduce iron-related nausea and stomach discomfort.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"59dbe5f6-0184-79af-a5dd-da2722639ef0\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Keep a journal to capture emotions, fears, questions, and milestones that photos alone cannot preserve.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"97f49124-75e3-7fb1-9205-3444500c8dfc\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Stop Googling symptoms at 2 a.m.; instead learn the true red flags (severe headache, vision changes, chest pain, breathing difficulty, sudden swelling, leaking) and rely on one trusted source rather than crowdsourced opinions.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"c7ebf55b-20cf-7847-b79c-27717f99ac75\", \"20d30df4-3381-7d51-bf3b-9d55dbf55070\", \"629724df-097b-7fbc-bd4e-8043aa2e7a64\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Learn what your body will actually do in labor - stages, contractions, and normal progression - to reduce fear and feel prepared.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"16bc9d5a-ca5e-7b42-86f4-25a2880e159d\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Train your pelvic floor for both strength and relaxation so you move from passenger to participant during birth.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"aae36a14-0570-75c5-88a4-48c13a0a35ec\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Start planning for postpartum now: recovery, sleep disruption, hormonal shif","ts, meals, practical help, and emotional support - not just baby supplies.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"34aa2767-db39-74c6-a142-8576d15bf63c\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notCovered\": [\n    \"The creator's background and transcript framing (Diana's bio).\",\n    \"The 'Own My Birth' course and other additional resources mentioned.\",\n    \"Trimester guidance beyond the first-trimester walking example, which is the only trimester detail in the outline.\"\n  ],\n  \"plannedSceneCount\": 11,\n  \"stylePackId\": \"everyday\",\n  \"stylePackReason\": \"Friendly geometric illustration and warm cobalt-mint palette suit practical, step-by-step everyday health guidance for adult learners.\",\n  \"soundBed\": \"morning-pad\",\n  \"soundBedReason\": \"Calm, warm tones match a reassuring maternal-health topic and keep the pacing gentle for a 5-minute explainer.\"\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":2815,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":21925,"service":"api","correlationId":"01a0ece2-fd2f-7533-9408-bed00830d7cb"}}
